# Build context for `packages/proxy` — the proxy builds from its own context
# (see tools/scripts/deploy.sh), so the repo-root .dockerignore does not apply
# here and, until 2026-07-30, nothing did.
#
# `target/` is 21GB. The Dockerfile never COPYs it — it takes only Cargo.toml,
# Cargo.lock, src/, build.rs, assets/ and benches/ — but Docker transfers the
# whole context to the daemon regardless of what the Dockerfile uses. So every
# proxy build moved 21GB to save reading a few megabytes of source.
target

# Prebuilt binaries: the image compiles from source in its builder stage and
# copies /build/target/release/intutic-proxy, so a host binary is never used.
bin

# Engineering notes and lockfile-adjacent files the build does not read.
*.md
.turbo
